-- title:
--   Lemma 4.2 — a local semimodularity test
-- statement:
--   Let $Q$ be a finite lattice, $J(Q)$ its nonzero join-irreducibles, $M(Q)$ its proper meet-irreducibles, and for $g \in J(Q)$ let $g_* = \bigvee\{i \in J(Q) : i < g\}$ be its lower cover. Suppose that for all $g, h \in J(Q)$ and $a, b \in M(Q)$,
--   $$g \not\le a,\ g \not\le b,\ g_* \le a,\ g_* \le b,\ h \le a,\ h \not\le b \ \Longrightarrow\ \exists p \in M(Q):\ g \le p,\ h \not\le p,\ a \wedge b \le p. \tag{4}$$
--   Then $Q$ is **upper semimodular**: whenever $a \wedge b$ is covered by $a$, $b$ is covered by $a \vee b$.
--
--   The lemma is the stopping certificate of the meet-irreducible enumeration of Theorem 4.1: a finite check on join- and meet-irreducibles that certifies semimodularity of the lattice generated by the elements found so far.
--
--   **Formalization Note.** $J(Q)$, $M(Q)$ are Mathlib's `SupIrred`, `InfIrred`; upper semimodularity is Mathlib's `IsUpperModularLattice` (`a ⊓ b ⋖ a → b ⋖ a ⊔ b`); a finite lattice is a `Lattice` with a `BoundedOrder` on a `Fintype`.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: a finite lattice, $J(Q)$, $M(Q)$, $g_*$, upper semimodular → `Lattice` + `BoundedOrder` + `Fintype`, `SupIrred`, `InfIrred`, `lowerStar` (formula (2)), `IsUpperModularLattice`; reason: Lean conventions for the same objects (a finite lattice is nonempty and bounded).
-- source:
--   Gkantzounis, Uniform Subpower Membership for Finite Mal'tsev Algebras, STOC 2027 submission (manuscript sha256 149e66b1…), p. 14, Lemma 4.2

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_UniformSubpower_Supplied_LatticeOracle

namespace UniformSubpower.Supplied

/-- Lemma 4.2 (Gkantzounis, p. 14): a local semimodularity test. `J(Q)` is `SupIrred`
(nonzero join-irreducibles), `M(Q)` is `InfIrred` (proper meet-irreducibles), `g∗` is
`lowerStar g`; upper semimodularity is Mathlib's `IsUpperModularLattice`
(`a ⊓ b ⋖ a → b ⋖ a ⊔ b`). -/
theorem lemma_4_2 {Q : Type*} [Lattice Q] [BoundedOrder Q] [Fintype Q]
    (h4 : ∀ g h a b : Q, SupIrred g → SupIrred h → InfIrred a → InfIrred b →
      ¬ g ≤ a → ¬ g ≤ b → lowerStar g ≤ a → lowerStar g ≤ b → h ≤ a → ¬ h ≤ b →
      ∃ p : Q, InfIrred p ∧ g ≤ p ∧ ¬ h ≤ p ∧ a ⊓ b ≤ p) :
    IsUpperModularLattice Q := by sorry

end UniformSubpower.Supplied
